{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://maxwell.onfinance.ai/schemas/v1/application/sbom-ref.schema.json",
  "title": "CycloneDX image SBOM",
  "description": "Validates applications/<app_id>/images/<image_id>.cdx.json, a CycloneDX 1.5, 1.6 or 1.7 JSON BOM produced by syft, trivy, cdxgen or a build plugin. This is a structural profile, not a re-implementation of the CycloneDX schema: it pins the fields Maxwell reads (bomFormat, specVersion, serialNumber, metadata.component, components, dependencies, vulnerabilities with VEX analysis) and closes the objects it defines. The remaining CycloneDX top-level sections (services, externalReferences, compositions, annotations, formulation, declarations, definitions, properties, signature, $schema) are enumerated with loose, size-capped subschemas because generators emit them and stripping them would break the BOM's own signature and downstream tooling; anything else is rejected. The BOM is an upstream format without a Maxwell provenance block, so the workflow that stores it must attribute it by adding metadata.properties entries named maxwell:runId, maxwell:sessionId, maxwell:workflow and maxwell:imageId (see the example); without them the SBOM cannot be tied to an audit run and KPIs are silently corrupted",
  "examples": [
    {
